  "basis": "The visual evidence confirms that Texas (TX) is colored pale yellow, corresponding to the 'High' end of the incidence scale (100), while Washington (WA) is colored dark burgundy, corresponding to the 'Low' end (0). Colorado (CO) is colored orange, indicating a mid-range incidence level. The legend explicitly maps dark burgundy to 'Low' (0) and pale yellow to 'High' (100). The workflow requires selecting the jurisdiction with the highest incidence, and only jurisdictions with comparable, encoded values can be compared. Since the gray fill of Colorado is not part of the incidence color scale and lacks a legend entry, it cannot be ranked. Therefore, the only comparable candidates are WA and TX, and TX has the highest displayed incidence.",
